---
description: TypeScript implementation conventions for orchestrator source and tests
globs: "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Prefer small modules with explicit responsibility boundaries.
- Keep public interfaces typed even where external CLI/protocol payloads require `any` at the edge.
- Normalize external payloads at adapter boundaries instead of leaking protocol-specific structures into the engine.
- Prefer Node standard library APIs for cross-platform operations.
- Do not add OS-specific shell assumptions to core code.
- Target ES2024 and strict NodeNext module resolution with explicit `.js` import extensions.
- Enforce `verbatimModuleSyntax: true`: use explicit `import type` annotations for all type-only imports.
- Maintain single-file transpilability (`isolatedModules: true`) and verify side-effect imports (`noUncheckedSideEffectImports: true`).
- Ambient type scopes are explicitly constrained via `types: ["node"]`.
- TSX rendering targets React 19 / Ink 7 via `jsx: "react-jsx"`.
